{"jobs":[{"id":"f54090ee-4305-4430-9266-23f2eab43d6f","title":"Founding BizOps (Apollo Unit)","department":"Founding Team","team":"Founding Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-19T21:13:40.457+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/f54090ee-4305-4430-9266-23f2eab43d6f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/f54090ee-4305-4430-9266-23f2eab43d6f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>The gap no one has filled</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. You have a lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that's arguably the most complex and touches every single family, leaves us on our own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population in the healthcare system. We’re covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Building the most trusted interface of healthcare</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are in the business of trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're designing for the most emotionally charged moments of our customers' lives; the bar isn't just delight, it's trust. Hera's brand promise is simple: care worthy of our parents. This promise is our moat.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's what physicians refer to, families buy, what Heroes deliver, and what the product must unlock and enforce at every touchpoint.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Our product challenge </h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The bottleneck isn't demand, it's supply. There aren't enough experts to serve every family who needs us. To scale to all of America, we have to unbundle expertise from the human so that anyone who can foster human connection can become a Hero. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The problem is that this expertise is tribal knowledge. One social worker knows how to expedite Medicaid in New York, another knows which home-visiting PT families actually love. It's trapped in people's heads.  </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To solve this,  our platform captures every interaction and turns it into compounding intelligence that makes every user smarter. Think Waymo: expert humans do the driving today, and every mile they log trains the system so that tomorrow, anyone — even with zero healthcare background — can perform like a 20-year veteran. The hard part is building a system that knows what to trust, what's gone stale, what's local versus universal, and how to surface the right insight at the right moment. Get it right and you've scaled healthcare expertise beyond the lucky few who know the right person.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.notion.site/what-endures-when-execution-is-free\">We wrote more on why and how we are building this technology here.</a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Our founding team</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'd revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us. <br />The customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. Along the way, we threw an art show for an 88 year old artist that <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time\">went viral</a> and a <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?igsh=MTR3cjg4ZmJvb2NyZQ%3D%3D\">talent show</a> where every act is over 65.<br />You’ll build Hera alongside co-founders <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/\">Jenny</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/\">Myles</a> &amp; <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/\">Connie</a> and a team from Palantir and Headway. We are in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.com/about\">here</a>.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Join our Apollo Unit to do hard things with us</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an ambitious and relentless generalist problem solver to join us on this mission. At other companies this role is often called Business Operations and Strategy. We call it Apollo Unit, drawing inspiration from the mythological figure, to represent the team ethos - surgical execution, relentless truth seeking, and obsession with greatness. You will go where Hera needs you the most, often into unknown terrains, and figure things out. Build the Hero growth engine. Launch new markets. Design systems to uphold quality. Build technology that feels human when humans are getting displaced by technology.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">When you solve a hard problem, you will know that you’ve empowered some of the most selfless members of our society to tangibly impact the lives of some of those most in need. You will also be rewarded with harder problems. Our promise is we will stretch your limits, and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes.</p><h2><br /><br />What we value</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Worthy of our parents: </strong>We don’t leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone’s mother. Quality isn’t a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration must be an accelerant. </strong>Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Celebrate human. </strong>Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enjoy the uphill. </strong>Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We’re excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb: figuring out how to take down the beast, one foot in front of the other. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attack. </strong>Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We’re here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If this excites you and these values speak to you, let’s talk: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:connie@hellohera.com\">connie@hellohera.com</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"THE GAP NO ONE HAS FILLED\n\nEvery complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. You have a lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that's arguably the most complex and touches every single family, leaves us on our own.\n\n99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population in the healthcare system. We’re covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.\n\n\n\n\nBUILDING THE MOST TRUSTED INTERFACE OF HEALTHCARE\n\nWe are in the business of trust.\n\nWe're designing for the most emotionally charged moments of our customers' lives; the bar isn't just delight, it's trust. Hera's brand promise is simple: care worthy of our parents. This promise is our moat.\n\nIt's what physicians refer to, families buy, what Heroes deliver, and what the product must unlock and enforce at every touchpoint.\n\n\n\n\nOUR PRODUCT CHALLENGE \n\nThe bottleneck isn't demand, it's supply. There aren't enough experts to serve every family who needs us. To scale to all of America, we have to unbundle expertise from the human so that anyone who can foster human connection can become a Hero. \n\nThe problem is that this expertise is tribal knowledge. One social worker knows how to expedite Medicaid in New York, another knows which home-visiting PT families actually love. It's trapped in people's heads.  \n\nTo solve this,  our platform captures every interaction and turns it into compounding intelligence that makes every user smarter. Think Waymo: expert humans do the driving today, and every mile they log trains the system so that tomorrow, anyone — even with zero healthcare background — can perform like a 20-year veteran. The hard part is building a system that knows what to trust, what's gone stale, what's local versus universal, and how to surface the right insight at the right moment. Get it right and you've scaled healthcare expertise beyond the lucky few who know the right person.\n\nWe wrote more on why and how we are building this technology here. https://hellohera.notion.site/what-endures-when-execution-is-free\n\n\n\n\nOUR FOUNDING TEAM\n\nWe've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'd revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us. \nThe customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. Along the way, we threw an art show for an 88 year old artist that went viral https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time and a talent show https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?igsh=MTR3cjg4ZmJvb2NyZQ%3D%3D where every act is over 65.\nYou’ll build Hera alongside co-founders Jenny https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/, Myles https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/ & Connie https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/ and a team from Palantir and Headway. We are in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video here https://hellohera.com/about.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJOIN OUR APOLLO UNIT TO DO HARD THINGS WITH US\n\nWe are looking for an ambitious and relentless generalist problem solver to join us on this mission. At other companies this role is often called Business Operations and Strategy. We call it Apollo Unit, drawing inspiration from the mythological figure, to represent the team ethos - surgical execution, relentless truth seeking, and obsession with greatness. You will go where Hera needs you the most, often into unknown terrains, and figure things out. Build the Hero growth engine. Launch new markets. Design systems to uphold quality. Build technology that feels human when humans are getting displaced by technology.\n\nWhen you solve a hard problem, you will know that you’ve empowered some of the most selfless members of our society to tangibly impact the lives of some of those most in need. You will also be rewarded with harder problems. Our promise is we will stretch your limits, and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Worthy of our parents: We don’t leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone’s mother. Quality isn’t a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy. \n\n - Collaboration must be an accelerant. Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward. \n\n - Celebrate human. Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.\n\n - Enjoy the uphill. Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We’re excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb: figuring out how to take down the beast, one foot in front of the other. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.\n\n - Attack. Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We’re here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.\n\nIf this excites you and these values speak to you, let’s talk: connie@hellohera.com.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$100K – $200K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$100K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d1f0e1f9-ded8-45b9-80f1-d20e85c2361d","tierSummary":"$100K – $200K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ae160aec-204c-4d63-9e04-820ac2420b71","summary":"$100K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"3aacd132-9fcd-4ec8-a1bf-b896d9083806","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"16b1c1e6-626c-4967-81c1-3d071d52235f","title":"Onboarding Guide (Patient Enrollment), Spanish/English Bilingual","department":"Onboarding","team":"Onboarding","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-10T21:07:38.507+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/16b1c1e6-626c-4967-81c1-3d071d52235f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/16b1c1e6-626c-4967-81c1-3d071d52235f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A doctor refers a family to Hera. They're cautiously optimistic but mostly overwhelmed - they've been bounced between systems, handed pamphlets, told to \"call this number.\" They don't know what geriatric care management is. They definitely don't know it's covered by Medicare. They're one confusing phone call away from saying \"never mind, we'll figure it out ourselves.\"</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're the reason they don't.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Onboarding Guide, you're the first voice a family hears from Hera. You help them understand how Hera competently cares for their parents, walk them through every step of getting started, and hand them off to their Hero feeling confident, heard, and ready. You're part closer, part concierge, part care coordinator. You just make the path so clear and the experience so easy that saying yes feels obvious.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of relationship-building and operations. You're selling, but what you're selling is something families genuinely need, and your job is to remove every obstacle between a referral and a first appointment. Missing paperwork, skeptical adult children, a patient who's never used a computer - you will get through whatever it takes so that the family can meet their Hero.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your mission as the Onboarding Guide</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're the reason families actually get help instead of falling through the cracks between referral and care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You aren’t just going through a motion. You're building trust with real families at a vulnerable moment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You own the full onboarding experience, no handing things off and hoping for the best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You leverage technology to make onboarding seamless, not a stack of faxes and voicemails</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Elevate your ceiling. We're early stage and growing fast - Guides joining now are shaping how every future family experiences Hera</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1099 flexibility, 30–40 hrs/week in business hours EST (you set your schedule)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$25-30/hour base + enrollment bonuses (<strong>top performers earn $40-50/hour</strong>)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must be fluent in both<strong> Spanish and English</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the first point of contact after a doctor refers a family to Hera - guide them from \"what is Hera?\" to their first Hero appointment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote - must be located in the United States</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll actually do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Convert referrals into active clients by helping families understand what Hera is and how we can be valuable in their care journey</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide families through the onboarding process - paperwork, documentation, insurance verification, scheduling - so nothing stalls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate between families and Hera's care team to ensure a clean handoff to their matched Hero</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help families navigate technology: uploading documents, joining telehealth appointments, signing e-forms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spot friction in the intake process and fix it - not just for one family, but for every family after them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with our engineering team to streamline workflows and scale how many families we can onboard without sacrificing quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'd be a great fit if you</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have a background in healthcare sales, care coordination, or customer success — especially with older adults or their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are warm on the phone and sharp on the follow-through. Families trust you quickly and nothing falls through the cracks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Think \"how do I get this from 2 hours to 15 minutes\" without cutting corners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold yourself to a high bar: done right, not just done</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are tech-savvy and energized by fast-moving environments where the playbook is still being written</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're on a mission to change the way we care for our parents and redefine a universal human experience. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUGD6cawQfk\">Watch our launch video here.</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"A doctor refers a family to Hera. They're cautiously optimistic but mostly overwhelmed - they've been bounced between systems, handed pamphlets, told to \"call this number.\" They don't know what geriatric care management is. They definitely don't know it's covered by Medicare. They're one confusing phone call away from saying \"never mind, we'll figure it out ourselves.\"\n\nYou're the reason they don't.\n\nAs an Onboarding Guide, you're the first voice a family hears from Hera. You help them understand how Hera competently cares for their parents, walk them through every step of getting started, and hand them off to their Hero feeling confident, heard, and ready. You're part closer, part concierge, part care coordinator. You just make the path so clear and the experience so easy that saying yes feels obvious.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of relationship-building and operations. You're selling, but what you're selling is something families genuinely need, and your job is to remove every obstacle between a referral and a first appointment. Missing paperwork, skeptical adult children, a patient who's never used a computer - you will get through whatever it takes so that the family can meet their Hero.\n\nYour mission as the Onboarding Guide\n\n - You're the reason families actually get help instead of falling through the cracks between referral and care\n\n - You aren’t just going through a motion. You're building trust with real families at a vulnerable moment\n\n - You own the full onboarding experience, no handing things off and hoping for the best\n\n - You leverage technology to make onboarding seamless, not a stack of faxes and voicemails\n\n - Elevate your ceiling. We're early stage and growing fast - Guides joining now are shaping how every future family experiences Hera\n\nThe Role\n\n - 1099 flexibility, 30–40 hrs/week in business hours EST (you set your schedule)\n\n - $25-30/hour base + enrollment bonuses (top performers earn $40-50/hour)\n\n - Must be fluent in both Spanish and English\n\n - Be the first point of contact after a doctor refers a family to Hera - guide them from \"what is Hera?\" to their first Hero appointment\n\n - Remote - must be located in the United States\n\nWhat you'll actually do\n\n - Convert referrals into active clients by helping families understand what Hera is and how we can be valuable in their care journey\n\n - Guide families through the onboarding process - paperwork, documentation, insurance verification, scheduling - so nothing stalls\n\n - Coordinate between families and Hera's care team to ensure a clean handoff to their matched Hero\n\n - Help families navigate technology: uploading documents, joining telehealth appointments, signing e-forms\n\n - Spot friction in the intake process and fix it - not just for one family, but for every family after them\n\n - Collaborate with our engineering team to streamline workflows and scale how many families we can onboard without sacrificing quality\n\nYou'd be a great fit if you\n\n - Have a background in healthcare sales, care coordination, or customer success — especially with older adults or their families\n\n - Are warm on the phone and sharp on the follow-through. Families trust you quickly and nothing falls through the cracks\n\n - Think \"how do I get this from 2 hours to 15 minutes\" without cutting corners\n\n - Hold yourself to a high bar: done right, not just done\n\n - Are tech-savvy and energized by fast-moving environments where the playbook is still being written\n\nWe're on a mission to change the way we care for our parents and redefine a universal human experience. Watch our launch video here. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUGD6cawQfk","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$25 – $50 per hour • Top performers earn $40-50 / hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"d9be0fc3-bfe5-4033-b591-a837b15c3ac5","tierSummary":"base + enrollment bonus $25 – $50 per hour • Top performers earn $40-50 / hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":"Top performers earn $40-50 / hour","components":[{"id":"d101a90d-6e32-4852-9c74-1fdc5a7329c0","summary":"base + enrollment bonus $25 – $50 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":50}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":50}]}},{"id":"a12ea72b-85ed-4afe-8ccd-608c9f6f829c","title":"Founding Partnerships (Evangelist)","department":"Founding Team","team":"Founding Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-04T22:29:13.005+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/a12ea72b-85ed-4afe-8ccd-608c9f6f829c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/a12ea72b-85ed-4afe-8ccd-608c9f6f829c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>The gap no one has filled</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We’re covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Building healthcare's most trusted interface</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are in the business of trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're designing for the most emotionally charged moments of our customers' lives. Hera's brand promise is simple: care worthy of our parents. This promise is our moat. It's what physicians refer to, families buy, what Heroes deliver, and what the product must unlock and enforce at every touchpoint.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Our founding team</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised 34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10’xed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us. <br />The customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. Along the way, we threw an art show for an 88 year old artist that <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time\">went viral</a> and a <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?igsh=MTR3cjg4ZmJvb2NyZQ%3D%3D\">talent show</a> where every act is over 65.<br />You’ll build Hera alongside co-founders <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/\">Jenny</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/\">Myles</a> &amp; <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/\">Connie</a> and a team from Palantir and Headway. We are in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.com/about\">here</a>.</p><h2><br />The role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're calling this role Founding Partnerships (Evangelist) for a reason. This isn't conventional. We're convincing geriatricians, social workers, nurses, population health leaders, and health system executives to entrust us with their most vulnerable patients. The only way that works is if the person across the table believes, in their bones, that we will care for those patients better than anyone else. Evangelism is the right word because the work is half conviction, half craft.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>From day 1, you own the health system referral engine. </strong>This is an IC-first role. That means mapping out the ecosystem of partners: who refers, who champions, and what each persona cares about. You'll build and run outreach to new health systems in New York, New Jersey, and in our national expansion. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll build the playbook ... and invent what hasn't been done.</strong> Some of what works will look like classic BD: stakeholder mapping, in-services, executive relationships. But some of the most powerful things we've done don't look like sales at all. This summer we're throwing a talent show called Encore where every performer is over 75, a community event that's also a partnership wedge. We want someone who can think from first principles and find creative ways to stand out and scale. The best ideas in this role probably aren't in any sales playbook you've read.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partners trust you fast. </strong>You genuinely give a damn about this mission and people can feel that. Partners refer to us because they believe we'll take care of their patients; that belief lives in you first.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You are absolutely relentless, but never transactional. </strong>You play the long game. You'll engineer an introduction over weeks or find the most unconventional way in. You treat \"no\" as information, not an answer. But every move is in service of building trust that lasts. Partners trust you because they can feel that you're not just trying to close them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You can deeply read people.</strong> You have a strong read on what someone actually wants or the hesitation they haven't said out loud and find the right thread to pull. You move people not by pushing harder but by understanding them better. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a builder. </strong>You thrive bringing clarity to ambiguity. You're rigorous about what's working and what's not. You track your own metrics and iterate without being told.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Based in NYC</strong> or willing to relocate.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>What we value</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Worthy of our parents: </strong>We don’t leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone’s mother. Quality isn’t a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration must be an accelerant. </strong>Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Celebrate human. </strong>Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enjoy the uphill. </strong>Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We’re excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb: figuring out how to take down the beast, one foot in front of the other. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attack. </strong>Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We’re here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:jenny@hellohera.com\">jenny@hellohera.com</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THE GAP NO ONE HAS FILLED\n\nEvery complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.\n\n99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We’re covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.\n\n \n\n\nBUILDING HEALTHCARE'S MOST TRUSTED INTERFACE\n\nWe are in the business of trust.\n\nWe're designing for the most emotionally charged moments of our customers' lives. Hera's brand promise is simple: care worthy of our parents. This promise is our moat. It's what physicians refer to, families buy, what Heroes deliver, and what the product must unlock and enforce at every touchpoint.\n\n \n\n\nOUR FOUNDING TEAM\n\nWe've raised 34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10’xed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us. \nThe customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. Along the way, we threw an art show for an 88 year old artist that went viral https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time and a talent show https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?igsh=MTR3cjg4ZmJvb2NyZQ%3D%3D where every act is over 65.\nYou’ll build Hera alongside co-founders Jenny https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/, Myles https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/ & Connie https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/ and a team from Palantir and Headway. We are in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video here https://hellohera.com/about.\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe're calling this role Founding Partnerships (Evangelist) for a reason. This isn't conventional. We're convincing geriatricians, social workers, nurses, population health leaders, and health system executives to entrust us with their most vulnerable patients. The only way that works is if the person across the table believes, in their bones, that we will care for those patients better than anyone else. Evangelism is the right word because the work is half conviction, half craft.\n\n - From day 1, you own the health system referral engine. This is an IC-first role. That means mapping out the ecosystem of partners: who refers, who champions, and what each persona cares about. You'll build and run outreach to new health systems in New York, New Jersey, and in our national expansion. \n\n - You'll build the playbook ... and invent what hasn't been done. Some of what works will look like classic BD: stakeholder mapping, in-services, executive relationships. But some of the most powerful things we've done don't look like sales at all. This summer we're throwing a talent show called Encore where every performer is over 75, a community event that's also a partnership wedge. We want someone who can think from first principles and find creative ways to stand out and scale. The best ideas in this role probably aren't in any sales playbook you've read.\n\n \n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - Partners trust you fast. You genuinely give a damn about this mission and people can feel that. Partners refer to us because they believe we'll take care of their patients; that belief lives in you first.\n\n - You are absolutely relentless, but never transactional. You play the long game. You'll engineer an introduction over weeks or find the most unconventional way in. You treat \"no\" as information, not an answer. But every move is in service of building trust that lasts. Partners trust you because they can feel that you're not just trying to close them.\n\n - You can deeply read people. You have a strong read on what someone actually wants or the hesitation they haven't said out loud and find the right thread to pull. You move people not by pushing harder but by understanding them better. \n\n - You're a builder. You thrive bringing clarity to ambiguity. You're rigorous about what's working and what's not. You track your own metrics and iterate without being told.\n\n - Based in NYC or willing to relocate.\n   \n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Worthy of our parents: We don’t leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone’s mother. Quality isn’t a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy. \n\n - Collaboration must be an accelerant. Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward. \n\n - Celebrate human. Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.\n\n - Enjoy the uphill. Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We’re excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb: figuring out how to take down the beast, one foot in front of the other. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.\n\n - Attack. Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We’re here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.\n\n \n\nOur promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: jenny@hellohera.com","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$100K – $250K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$100K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a6ba61e5-26c8-4e26-ab28-c801e3e326f3","tierSummary":"$100K – $250K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3b0adc4b-0311-41c6-b5b8-69ed9964879b","summary":"$100K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"a3db552b-b609-43eb-a989-ced9b5541716","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cbc881cd-1940-46ce-8be2-68b329c35661","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"fb797d93-7647-4055-98e1-1d108ded36dd","title":"Hera Hero","department":"Heroes","team":"Heroes","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-18T20:24:09.684+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/fb797d93-7647-4055-98e1-1d108ded36dd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/fb797d93-7647-4055-98e1-1d108ded36dd/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is not a typical social work or nursing role.</strong> If you've felt that traditional healthcare roles have a ceiling on you, and you want to actually bridge the gaps for older adults after they leave the office or facility, Hera is for you.<br /><br />An older adult gets discharged from the hospital and you already know they'll be back in 30 days. A family leaves overwhelmed, clutching a stack of papers with numbers they'll never get through. You did everything you could within the system and it <em>still wasn't enough</em>. We started Hera because we felt the system was letting down the generation that raised us. <br /><br /><strong>Hera is dedicated care management in the community for older adults, covered by Medicare.</strong> Every family gets matched with a dedicated Hero, you, who actually has the tools, time, and autonomy to help. It’s not a 15 min monthly check-in call. It’s real, ongoing support where you see things through and families call you their Hero.<br /><br /><strong>Why Heroes tell us this feels different</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Autonomy</strong> to manage your own client load: you own your families to give them the care they deserve instead of hoping for the best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Remote work from home</strong>, set your own flexible schedule</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Delightful technology</strong> built for you so you can focus on fostering connection with families, not fighting an EMR</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're never alone on a case</strong> with supportive training and community of other Heroes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>No ceiling on you</strong>. We're early stage and growing fast, Heroes joining now are shaping the company.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1099, 30–40 hrs/week in business hours (you set your schedule)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$30–60 / hour: factors include experience, geography, and client load</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve older adults and their families in aging at home safely</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'd be a great fit if you are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold an LMSW, LCSW, or RN (not required but a plus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have experience in geriatric care management, hospice, palliative care, discharge planning, rehab, or hospital social work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Love fostering connection with older adults and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are a creative problem solver who wants a job that looks different every day</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are tech-savvy and excited by quickly evolving environments and leveraging AI to supercharge your work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote - must be located in the United States</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>We’re on a mission to change the way we care for our parents and redefine a universal human experience. </strong><br /><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUGD6cawQfk\">Watch our launch video here.</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"This is not a typical social work or nursing role. If you've felt that traditional healthcare roles have a ceiling on you, and you want to actually bridge the gaps for older adults after they leave the office or facility, Hera is for you.\n\nAn older adult gets discharged from the hospital and you already know they'll be back in 30 days. A family leaves overwhelmed, clutching a stack of papers with numbers they'll never get through. You did everything you could within the system and it still wasn't enough. We started Hera because we felt the system was letting down the generation that raised us. \n\nHera is dedicated care management in the community for older adults, covered by Medicare. Every family gets matched with a dedicated Hero, you, who actually has the tools, time, and autonomy to help. It’s not a 15 min monthly check-in call. It’s real, ongoing support where you see things through and families call you their Hero.\n\nWhy Heroes tell us this feels different\n\n - Autonomy to manage your own client load: you own your families to give them the care they deserve instead of hoping for the best\n\n - Remote work from home, set your own flexible schedule\n\n - Delightful technology built for you so you can focus on fostering connection with families, not fighting an EMR\n\n - You're never alone on a case with supportive training and community of other Heroes\n\n - No ceiling on you. We're early stage and growing fast, Heroes joining now are shaping the company.\n\nThe Role\n\n - 1099, 30–40 hrs/week in business hours (you set your schedule)\n\n - $30–60 / hour: factors include experience, geography, and client load\n\n - Serve older adults and their families in aging at home safely\n\nYou'd be a great fit if you are\n\n - Hold an LMSW, LCSW, or RN (not required but a plus)\n\n - Have experience in geriatric care management, hospice, palliative care, discharge planning, rehab, or hospital social work\n\n - Love fostering connection with older adults and their families\n\n - Are a creative problem solver who wants a job that looks different every day\n\n - Are tech-savvy and excited by quickly evolving environments and leveraging AI to supercharge your work\n\n - Remote - must be located in the United States\n\n\nWe’re on a mission to change the way we care for our parents and redefine a universal human experience. \nWatch our launch video here. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUGD6cawQfk","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$30 – $60 per hour • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"61967543-4d9c-4fb1-a7bd-4f00e8624a49","tierSummary":"$30 – $60 per hour • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3521f5a8-c4d7-41a7-892e-a14b31d1842a","summary":"$30 – $60 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":30,"maxValue":60},{"id":"ed71ca37-5c40-4f56-a72e-d883b6529335","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":30,"maxValue":60},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2e343c29-9f92-497a-b290-eee01b6c278c","title":"Founding Engineer","department":"Founding Team","team":"Founding Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-01T17:13:08.748+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/2e343c29-9f92-497a-b290-eee01b6c278c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/2e343c29-9f92-497a-b290-eee01b6c278c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The gap no one has filled</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. You have a lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that's arguably the most complex and touches every single family, leaves us on our own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population in the healthcare system. We’re covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Building the most trusted interface of healthcare</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are in the business of trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're designing for the most emotionally charged moments of our customers' lives. The bar isn't just delight, it's trust. Hera's brand promise is simple: care that would only be great enough for our own parents. This promise is our moat.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's what physicians refer to, families buy, what Heroes deliver, and what the product must unlock and enforce at every touchpoint.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The supply challenge</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">There aren't enough experts to serve every family who needs us. The bottleneck isn't demand, it's supply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In order to scale to all of America, we need to unbundle expertise from the human and broaden the aperture of who can become a Hero. Anyone that can foster human connection should be able to become a Hero with Hera. In that world, our supply challenge becomes how we uphold our brand promise across every touchpoint with our customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Our product challenge</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe the best software is invisible. We serve people most technology overlooks: social workers, nurses, aging parents, and their families. Every interaction builds or breaks trust, so our product must help Heroes deliver expert-level care at every moment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare navigation depends on tribal knowledge. One social worker knows how to expedite Medicaid in New York, while another knows which physical therapist families trust. This expertise is valuable but fragmented. We are building the product that brings it together.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our platform captures interactions, solved problems, and insights from expert care managers, turning them into shared intelligence. Over time, this knowledge helps every user make better decisions and enables people with limited healthcare experience to work with the judgment of seasoned professionals. The goal is to build a trusted knowledge system that understands what is reliable, current, local, and relevant, then surfaces the right insight at the right time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Our founding team</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We closed a 7M seed round led by Accel and 10’xed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, and Mount Sinai. We’ve been doing fun things in the community along the way (threw an art show for an 88 year old artist that <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time\"><em><u>went viral</u></em></a>) and the customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. You’ll build Hera alongside co-founders <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/\"><u>Jenny</u></a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/\"><u>Myles</u></a> &amp; <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/\"><u>Connie</u></a> and a team from Headway and Palantir. We are in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.com/about\"><u>here</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In a world of growing cynicism we chase hard truths, give a damn, and build.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our entire team believes truth is in the field. This means we are side by side with our Heroes everyday, learning what it takes to do the job and do it well.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are high autonomy and trust. There is no space for micromanagement, if you see a problem or think of a solution, you are empowered to run at it wholeheartedly and know that the team has your back.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are creative in our bones. For the first time in many years, we are seeing the genesis of a new profession of a profound scale and importance; it’s on us to define what it can and should look like.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join our Founding Team to impact real lives</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for ambitious and relentless engineers to join us on this mission. Whereas at other companies you may be working on the next widget, analytics suite, dev tooling, or b2b revolution, what we are trying to do is as tangible as it gets. We serve the everyday people in society that are most sorely in need of help and who have been least addressed by the technological revolution and developer brainpower of the past decades. We want to bring the highest quality builders to bear on this.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">When you solve a hard problem, you will know that you’ve empowered some of the most selfless members of our society to tangibly impact the lives of some of those most in need. You will also be rewarded with harder problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our promise is we will stretch your limits, and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring for a founding software engineer to help build Hera end to end, spanning the backend systems and frontend experiences that power our care platform. This is a founding role for an engineer who cares deeply about sound systems design, product quality, thoughtful user experience, and getting the details right in an environment where trust, data sensitivity, and operational correctness matter.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design and build core backend systems.</strong> You will architect and implement the infrastructure, services, APIs, and internal platform capabilities that underpin Hera’s product and operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and build core frontend product experiences.</strong> You will design and implement key workflows across Hera’s product and help shape how the platform feels and functions day to day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build for reliability and correctness.</strong> You will create systems that are fault-tolerant, idempotent, and thoughtfully designed to handle sensitive workflows safely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Translate craft and taste into product quality.</strong> You will bring a strong point of view on interaction design, UI polish, and overall product quality, and hold a high standard for what ships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work closely with users.</strong> You will stay grounded in the lived reality of Heroes, families, and internal users, and use those insights to build with context rather than in a vacuum.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own critical data and infrastructure decisions.</strong> You will help shape how Hera handles complex workflows involving medical, billing, operational, and user data across the platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Help set engineering standards.</strong> You will contribute to code quality, system cleanliness, testing, performance, service architecture, and a thoughtful engineering culture as an early member of the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operate with high autonomy.</strong> You will identify opportunities, move quickly, and take ownership without needing heavy direction or hand-holding.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong backend, infrastructure, and frontend fundamentals.</strong> You have experience designing sound systems and building high-quality product experiences with strong performance, maintainability, and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design-minded product strength.</strong> You have a clear appreciation for product craft, interaction design, UI polish, and user experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Taste and creativity.</strong> You have experience building products that feel intentional and polished, and you care deeply about how software looks and feels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>User proximity.</strong> You are excited by direct engagement with users and want to build informed by real-world behavior and needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Security and compliance awareness.</strong> Experience working with permissions, role-based access controls, security-sensitive flows, compliance-minded systems, or other trust-critical infrastructure is a major plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ownership and autonomy.</strong> You are self-directed, opinionated in a healthy way, and excited to take responsibility for major technical and product decisions as an early engineer.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relevant technical fluency.</strong> TypeScript, React, Next.js, AWS or similar cloud infrastructure, SQL and non-SQL databases, consumer-scale APIs, SDKs, service-oriented architecture, and comfort with modern AI-native workflows are all highly relevant.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We pay at the top of market with founding-level equity. People who deliver outsized outcomes should be rewarded with outsized upside.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"The gap no one has filled\n\nEvery complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. You have a lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that's arguably the most complex and touches every single family, leaves us on our own.\n\n99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population in the healthcare system. We’re covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.\n\n\n\nBuilding the most trusted interface of healthcare\n\nWe are in the business of trust.\n\nWe're designing for the most emotionally charged moments of our customers' lives. The bar isn't just delight, it's trust. Hera's brand promise is simple: care that would only be great enough for our own parents. This promise is our moat.\n\nIt's what physicians refer to, families buy, what Heroes deliver, and what the product must unlock and enforce at every touchpoint.\n\n\n\nThe supply challenge\n\nThere aren't enough experts to serve every family who needs us. The bottleneck isn't demand, it's supply.\n\nIn order to scale to all of America, we need to unbundle expertise from the human and broaden the aperture of who can become a Hero. Anyone that can foster human connection should be able to become a Hero with Hera. In that world, our supply challenge becomes how we uphold our brand promise across every touchpoint with our customers.\n\n\n\nOur product challenge\n\nWe believe the best software is invisible. We serve people most technology overlooks: social workers, nurses, aging parents, and their families. Every interaction builds or breaks trust, so our product must help Heroes deliver expert-level care at every moment.\n\nHealthcare navigation depends on tribal knowledge. One social worker knows how to expedite Medicaid in New York, while another knows which physical therapist families trust. This expertise is valuable but fragmented. We are building the product that brings it together.\n\nOur platform captures interactions, solved problems, and insights from expert care managers, turning them into shared intelligence. Over time, this knowledge helps every user make better decisions and enables people with limited healthcare experience to work with the judgment of seasoned professionals. The goal is to build a trusted knowledge system that understands what is reliable, current, local, and relevant, then surfaces the right insight at the right time.\n\n\n\nOur founding team\n\nWe closed a 7M seed round led by Accel and 10’xed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, and Mount Sinai. We’ve been doing fun things in the community along the way (threw an art show for an 88 year old artist that went viral https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time) and the customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. You’ll build Hera alongside co-founders Jenny https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/, Myles https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/ & Connie https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/ and a team from Headway and Palantir. We are in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video here https://hellohera.com/about.\n\n\n\nIn a world of growing cynicism we chase hard truths, give a damn, and build.\n\nOur entire team believes truth is in the field. This means we are side by side with our Heroes everyday, learning what it takes to do the job and do it well.\n\nWe are high autonomy and trust. There is no space for micromanagement, if you see a problem or think of a solution, you are empowered to run at it wholeheartedly and know that the team has your back.\n\nWe are creative in our bones. For the first time in many years, we are seeing the genesis of a new profession of a profound scale and importance; it’s on us to define what it can and should look like.\n\nJoin our Founding Team to impact real lives\n\nWe are looking for ambitious and relentless engineers to join us on this mission. Whereas at other companies you may be working on the next widget, analytics suite, dev tooling, or b2b revolution, what we are trying to do is as tangible as it gets. We serve the everyday people in society that are most sorely in need of help and who have been least addressed by the technological revolution and developer brainpower of the past decades. We want to bring the highest quality builders to bear on this.\n\nWhen you solve a hard problem, you will know that you’ve empowered some of the most selfless members of our society to tangibly impact the lives of some of those most in need. You will also be rewarded with harder problems.\n\nOur promise is we will stretch your limits, and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes.\n\n\n\nThe role\n\nWe are hiring for a founding software engineer to help build Hera end to end, spanning the backend systems and frontend experiences that power our care platform. This is a founding role for an engineer who cares deeply about sound systems design, product quality, thoughtful user experience, and getting the details right in an environment where trust, data sensitivity, and operational correctness matter.\n\nWhat you'll do\n\n - Design and build core backend systems. You will architect and implement the infrastructure, services, APIs, and internal platform capabilities that underpin Hera’s product and operations.\n\n - Own and build core frontend product experiences. You will design and implement key workflows across Hera’s product and help shape how the platform feels and functions day to day.\n\n - Build for reliability and correctness. You will create systems that are fault-tolerant, idempotent, and thoughtfully designed to handle sensitive workflows safely.\n\n - Translate craft and taste into product quality. You will bring a strong point of view on interaction design, UI polish, and overall product quality, and hold a high standard for what ships.\n\n - Work closely with users. You will stay grounded in the lived reality of Heroes, families, and internal users, and use those insights to build with context rather than in a vacuum.\n\n - Own critical data and infrastructure decisions. You will help shape how Hera handles complex workflows involving medical, billing, operational, and user data across the platform.\n\n - Help set engineering standards. You will contribute to code quality, system cleanliness, testing, performance, service architecture, and a thoughtful engineering culture as an early member of the team.\n\n - Operate with high autonomy. You will identify opportunities, move quickly, and take ownership without needing heavy direction or hand-holding.\n   \n   \n\nWhat we are looking for\n\n - Strong backend, infrastructure, and frontend fundamentals. You have experience designing sound systems and building high-quality product experiences with strong performance, maintainability, and attention to detail.\n\n - Design-minded product strength. You have a clear appreciation for product craft, interaction design, UI polish, and user experience.\n\n - Taste and creativity. You have experience building products that feel intentional and polished, and you care deeply about how software looks and feels.\n\n - User proximity. You are excited by direct engagement with users and want to build informed by real-world behavior and needs.\n\n - Security and compliance awareness. Experience working with permissions, role-based access controls, security-sensitive flows, compliance-minded systems, or other trust-critical infrastructure is a major plus.\n\n - Ownership and autonomy. You are self-directed, opinionated in a healthy way, and excited to take responsibility for major technical and product decisions as an early engineer.\n\n - Relevant technical fluency. TypeScript, React, Next.js, AWS or similar cloud infrastructure, SQL and non-SQL databases, consumer-scale APIs, SDKs, service-oriented architecture, and comfort with modern AI-native workflows are all highly relevant.\n\n\n\nCompensation\n\nWe pay at the top of market with founding-level equity. People who deliver outsized outcomes should be rewarded with outsized upside.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4fd62956-7a4e-4177-b62f-0cfe6ab08bd8","tierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0e6cbefa-e514-4f3d-9fde-3d6358847eac","summary":"$200K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"6b1dd298-d1aa-4f88-a5e2-cd10d723771c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"58d2fe4d-078e-4234-8d60-83045c877238","title":"Telemedicine Physician, 50-State Licensed — Geriatric Care","department":"Clinical","team":"Clinical","employmentType":"PartTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-07T00:45:40.389+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/58d2fe4d-078e-4234-8d60-83045c877238","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/58d2fe4d-078e-4234-8d60-83045c877238/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><u>This is not a typical physician role. </u></strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you've felt that traditional healthcare pressures clinicians to churn volume and don't actually shape patient outcomes, Hera is for you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An older adult gets discharged from the hospital—you already know what happens. The family scrambles. Nobody talks to each other. Medications get confused. A fall happens. Another admission. The system wasn't designed for this moment. We started Hera because we felt it wasn't enough.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hera is dedicated care management in the community for older adults, covered by Medicare.</strong> Every family gets matched with a dedicated Hero (care manager) who has the tools, time, and autonomy to deliver ongoing support. You're the clinical entry point—the comprehensive assessment that sets the clinical foundation for real, ongoing intervention.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><u>The Role</u></strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building the clinical infrastructure that makes great geriatric care exceptional. As a Clinical MD, you'll conduct telehealth assessments that serve as the clinical gateway for families newly enrolled with Hera. Each 45-60 minute visit establishes the clinical foundation: confirming Medicare eligibility, synthesizing complex medical and social history, identifying barriers to treatment, and flagging clinical priorities for our care managers (Heroes) to address over months of ongoing coordination. This assessment work directly shapes the care strategy that families receive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><u>Key Responsibilities</u></strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Conduct comprehensive telehealth assessments for newly enrolled Medicare clients</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Synthesize complex medical histories and identify clinical priorities for ongoing care coordination</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Document clinical findings that inform care manager (Hero) intervention strategies</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Provide clinical oversight and collaboration as needed with care management team</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Establish clinical credibility and trust during initial patient contact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><u>Why clinicians tell us Hera feels different</u></strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Clinical autonomy.</strong> You own your assessments. No templates, no utilization pressure, no inbox drowning. You conduct real clinical work that shapes care plans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Remote work from home.</strong> Set your own flexible schedule. No clinic overhead, no commute, no admin burden.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>You're building it.</strong> You're not an employee in a machine. You're a founding clinical leader shaping how we do geriatric care in new states.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>You're never alone on a case.</strong> A whole care team (Heroes, social workers, coordinators) executes the plan you establish. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>No ceiling on you.</strong> We're early stage and growing fast. Clinical leaders joining now are shaping the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><u>Requirements</u></strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• MD or DO <strong>(must be licensed to practice in all 50 states)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Board certification in family medicine, internal medicine or other relevant speciality.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Substantial experience in geriatric medicine, primary care, or chronic disease management</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Confident in telehealth assessment and skilled at building clinical rapport across a screen</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Strong clinical judgment and comfort with complexity and ambiguity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Aligned with our mission: you see older adults as deserving of excellent, attentive care</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ready to shape geriatric care delivery at scale? Apply now.</p>","descriptionPlain":"This is not a typical physician role. \n\nIf you've felt that traditional healthcare pressures clinicians to churn volume and don't actually shape patient outcomes, Hera is for you.\n\n \n\nAn older adult gets discharged from the hospital—you already know what happens. The family scrambles. Nobody talks to each other. Medications get confused. A fall happens. Another admission. The system wasn't designed for this moment. We started Hera because we felt it wasn't enough.\n\n \n\nHera is dedicated care management in the community for older adults, covered by Medicare. Every family gets matched with a dedicated Hero (care manager) who has the tools, time, and autonomy to deliver ongoing support. You're the clinical entry point—the comprehensive assessment that sets the clinical foundation for real, ongoing intervention.\n\n\n\nThe Role\n\nWe're building the clinical infrastructure that makes great geriatric care exceptional. As a Clinical MD, you'll conduct telehealth assessments that serve as the clinical gateway for families newly enrolled with Hera. Each 45-60 minute visit establishes the clinical foundation: confirming Medicare eligibility, synthesizing complex medical and social history, identifying barriers to treatment, and flagging clinical priorities for our care managers (Heroes) to address over months of ongoing coordination. This assessment work directly shapes the care strategy that families receive.\n\n \n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Conduct comprehensive telehealth assessments for newly enrolled Medicare clients\n\n• Synthesize complex medical histories and identify clinical priorities for ongoing care coordination\n\n• Document clinical findings that inform care manager (Hero) intervention strategies\n\n• Provide clinical oversight and collaboration as needed with care management team\n\n• Establish clinical credibility and trust during initial patient contact\n\n\n\nWhy clinicians tell us Hera feels different\n\n• Clinical autonomy. You own your assessments. No templates, no utilization pressure, no inbox drowning. You conduct real clinical work that shapes care plans.\n\n• Remote work from home. Set your own flexible schedule. No clinic overhead, no commute, no admin burden.\n\n• You're building it. You're not an employee in a machine. You're a founding clinical leader shaping how we do geriatric care in new states.\n\n• You're never alone on a case. A whole care team (Heroes, social workers, coordinators) executes the plan you establish. \n\n• No ceiling on you. We're early stage and growing fast. Clinical leaders joining now are shaping the company.\n\n \n\nRequirements\n\n• MD or DO (must be licensed to practice in all 50 states)\n\n• Board certification in family medicine, internal medicine or other relevant speciality.\n\n• Substantial experience in geriatric medicine, primary care, or chronic disease management\n\n• Confident in telehealth assessment and skilled at building clinical rapport across a screen\n\n• Strong clinical judgment and comfort with complexity and ambiguity\n\n• Aligned with our mission: you see older adults as deserving of excellent, attentive care\n\n \n\nReady to shape geriatric care delivery at scale? Apply now.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150 – $250 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"ad3b8956-b361-45b0-9c45-dce063d3e2f2","tierSummary":"$150 – $250 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3de1e1cd-ff2c-4079-90b4-ef4d4f27d296","summary":"$150 – $250 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150,"maxValue":250}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150,"maxValue":250}]}},{"id":"59a984a1-ece4-4b88-a9ec-7f5cff58623b","title":"Chief Medical Officer","department":"Clinical","team":"Clinical","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-07T16:06:51.254+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/59a984a1-ece4-4b88-a9ec-7f5cff58623b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/59a984a1-ece4-4b88-a9ec-7f5cff58623b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>The gap no one has filled</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated care manager for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Quality is the strategy</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We serve the most complex, highest-acuity population in healthcare: older adults coming straight out of a hospital discharge, living with dementia, juggling a dozen medications and twice as many specialists. When families meet us, they are facing the hardest experience of their entire lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our brand promise is simple: care worthy of our parents. That promise is our moat. It's why physicians refer, why families join, and what every Hero must deliver on every visit.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are creating a new category. Winning is how we make sure the standard of care for this generation of parents is one worthy of them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">That is why this role exists. The Chief Medical Officer at Hera is the person who defines what great care means at Hera, and makes sure we deliver it for every family.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Our founding team</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'ed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll build Hera alongside co-founders Jenny, Myles &amp; Connie and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you would have equity in the company. We are in person in NYC. Read our story <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.com/about\">here</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are the clinical leader of Hera. From day one, the full care team — Heroes and their clinical supervisors — report to you, and clinicians practice under your medical direction. You own the standard of what worthy care looks like, how it's measured, and how it gets delivered. And you'll stay close to the work: you'll see patients occasionally, because the person setting the standard of care should never be far from the work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Three charters to start with: </p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the care model and run the care team.</strong> You define how Hera keeps clients safely at home and out of the hospital — what great care means for this population, how it's delivered consistently across every Hero, and how clinical oversight continues long past the first visit. You set the standard, you build the systems that measure it in partnership with engineering and ops, and when the bar isn't met, you're the one who acts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be the clinical brain of the product.</strong> Most clinical leaders write training modules and scale through rigid processes that allow things to slip through the cracks. You'll do something different: partner with our engineering team to encode clinical judgment directly into our AI platform so that quality scales through software, not headcount. This is the part of the job that has never existed before, and it's the reason the right person will find this the most interesting clinical role in the country.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Define and shape a new category.</strong> We meet most of our families through health systems. You make Hera the most credible clinical voice in the room with health system leaders and payers, and you turn our care model into the industry's reference point. Long-term, you help position Hera as the category creator in longitudinal care management: the missing piece of American healthcare.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1>Who you are</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a physician.</strong> MD required, board certified in internal medicine, geriatrics, or family medicine. You'll serve as medical director of record from day one. You hold an active, unrestricted license and can obtain licensure in additional states as we grow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've spent 7+ years caring for complex, high-acuity patients.</strong> Geriatrics is ideal, but what matters is that you deeply understand this population: hospital discharges, polypharmacy, dementia and what keeps them out of the hospital.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've led clinical teams and owned outcomes for 5+ years.</strong> You've built care models, protocols, and oversight systems, ideally at a tech-forward healthcare company, and managed clinicians and care teams at scale. You know how to earn the trust of nurses and social workers, and how to hold a bar without breaking a team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've delivered care beyond the four walls.</strong> You've built or run virtual, home-based, or hybrid care models and know how to maintain clinical quality when care happens over the phone, on video, and in living rooms, not just in clinic.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a builder, not a figure head.</strong> This is a 0→1 role. You'd rather define the rubric than inherit one. You're rigorous about what's working, obsessed with measurement, and willing to do the unglamorous work of getting the details right yourself.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You believe software is a clinical tool.</strong> You get genuinely excited about encoding your judgment into a product that makes every care manager perform like your best one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partners trust you fast.</strong> Health system executives, geriatricians, and payers walk away from a conversation with you believing their patients are safer with Hera.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideally based in NYC or willing to relocate.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What we value</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Worthy of our parents.</strong> We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration must be an accelerant.</strong> Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Celebrate human.</strong> Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enjoy the uphill.</strong> Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attack.</strong> Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:jenny@hellohera.com\">jenny@hellohera.com</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THE GAP NO ONE HAS FILLED\n\nEvery complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.\n\n99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated care manager for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.\n\n\n\n\nQUALITY IS THE STRATEGY\n\nWe serve the most complex, highest-acuity population in healthcare: older adults coming straight out of a hospital discharge, living with dementia, juggling a dozen medications and twice as many specialists. When families meet us, they are facing the hardest experience of their entire lives.\n\nOur brand promise is simple: care worthy of our parents. That promise is our moat. It's why physicians refer, why families join, and what every Hero must deliver on every visit.\n\nWe are creating a new category. Winning is how we make sure the standard of care for this generation of parents is one worthy of them.\n\nThat is why this role exists. The Chief Medical Officer at Hera is the person who defines what great care means at Hera, and makes sure we deliver it for every family.\n\n\n\n\nOUR FOUNDING TEAM\n\nWe've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'ed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.\n\nYou'll build Hera alongside co-founders Jenny, Myles & Connie and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you would have equity in the company. We are in person in NYC. Read our story here https://hellohera.com/about.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nYou are the clinical leader of Hera. From day one, the full care team — Heroes and their clinical supervisors — report to you, and clinicians practice under your medical direction. You own the standard of what worthy care looks like, how it's measured, and how it gets delivered. And you'll stay close to the work: you'll see patients occasionally, because the person setting the standard of care should never be far from the work.\n\n\n\nThree charters to start with: \n\n 1. Own the care model and run the care team. You define how Hera keeps clients safely at home and out of the hospital — what great care means for this population, how it's delivered consistently across every Hero, and how clinical oversight continues long past the first visit. You set the standard, you build the systems that measure it in partnership with engineering and ops, and when the bar isn't met, you're the one who acts.\n\n 2. Be the clinical brain of the product. Most clinical leaders write training modules and scale through rigid processes that allow things to slip through the cracks. You'll do something different: partner with our engineering team to encode clinical judgment directly into our AI platform so that quality scales through software, not headcount. This is the part of the job that has never existed before, and it's the reason the right person will find this the most interesting clinical role in the country.\n\n 3. Define and shape a new category. We meet most of our families through health systems. You make Hera the most credible clinical voice in the room with health system leaders and payers, and you turn our care model into the industry's reference point. Long-term, you help position Hera as the category creator in longitudinal care management: the missing piece of American healthcare.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You're a physician. MD required, board certified in internal medicine, geriatrics, or family medicine. You'll serve as medical director of record from day one. You hold an active, unrestricted license and can obtain licensure in additional states as we grow.\n\n - You've spent 7+ years caring for complex, high-acuity patients. Geriatrics is ideal, but what matters is that you deeply understand this population: hospital discharges, polypharmacy, dementia and what keeps them out of the hospital.\n\n - You've led clinical teams and owned outcomes for 5+ years. You've built care models, protocols, and oversight systems, ideally at a tech-forward healthcare company, and managed clinicians and care teams at scale. You know how to earn the trust of nurses and social workers, and how to hold a bar without breaking a team.\n\n - You've delivered care beyond the four walls. You've built or run virtual, home-based, or hybrid care models and know how to maintain clinical quality when care happens over the phone, on video, and in living rooms, not just in clinic.\n\n - You're a builder, not a figure head. This is a 0→1 role. You'd rather define the rubric than inherit one. You're rigorous about what's working, obsessed with measurement, and willing to do the unglamorous work of getting the details right yourself.\n\n - You believe software is a clinical tool. You get genuinely excited about encoding your judgment into a product that makes every care manager perform like your best one.\n\n - Partners trust you fast. Health system executives, geriatricians, and payers walk away from a conversation with you believing their patients are safer with Hera.\n\n - Ideally based in NYC or willing to relocate.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Worthy of our parents. We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.\n\n - Collaboration must be an accelerant. Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.\n\n - Celebrate human. Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.\n\n - Enjoy the uphill. Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.\n\n - Attack. Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.\n   \n\nOur promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: jenny@hellohera.com","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$300K – $400K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$300K - $400K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f70609fb-7981-4631-9d96-197b9a3ac4f7","tierSummary":"$300K – $400K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6249d227-461f-426d-8156-f5bd869e952e","summary":"$300K – $400K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":300000,"maxValue":400000},{"id":"4a6fbd1c-e08b-47df-a397-ee219e65086e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":300000,"maxValue":400000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f3bac8ee-497d-47c7-a679-a952532e5a02","title":"Founding Recruiter","department":"Founding Team","team":"Founding Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T03:20:04.633+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/f3bac8ee-497d-47c7-a679-a952532e5a02","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/f3bac8ee-497d-47c7-a679-a952532e5a02/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>The gap no one has filled</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated care manager for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The team is everything</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re cultivating a team that can run through walls together to take care of the generation that raised us. The DNA of our team and the bar we hold for each other will shape the trajectory of the company. You will craft every touchpoint our future team experiences and how they spend time getting to know us. This is one of the most important roles at the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our founding team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'ed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll build Hera alongside co-founders <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/\">Jenny</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/\">Myles</a> &amp; <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/conniejkang/\">Connie</a> and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you would have meaningful ownership in the company. We are in person in NYC. Read our story <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.com/about\">here</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are my right hand on talent. Recruiting at Hera isn't a support function, it's how we win. You'll sit close enough to the founders to know exactly why each role is critical, how our narrative is evolving week to week, and how to tell that story to the exact person we need in the room. When the pitch shifts, you shift with it. When a candidate hesitates, you know which thread to pull.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the entire funnel.</strong> Sourcing, screening, and closing end to end, across both technical and business roles. You run the process, you own the candidate experience, and you make every hiring manager better at their part of it. The founding team will stay deeply involved in hiring; your job is to multiply us, not replace us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hunt.</strong> We're still early in building our talent brand, which means the best people won't come to us, you go get them. You have real hunter DNA and you source in an AI-native way: you use every tool available to find, reach, and win people nobody else is finding. Volume without craft doesn't work here, and craft without volume doesn't either.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner on talent strategy.</strong> You help shape which roles we open, in what order, and what great looks like for each. You bring rigor to how we run loops, calibrate bars, make decisions, and you push back when we're wrong.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Make how we recruit as distinctive as what we're building.</strong> We've thrown a<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&amp;igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==\"> talent show where every act is over 65</a>, sold out all the work for a retired 88 year old who had never sold a piece of art until the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time\">art show</a> we threw him, are hosting a Dinner with Nonna series, and have many events coming up that helps us share our story with the world. These are also mediums to bring talent into our community. We want to partner to be unconventional and willing to try things other nobody else has tried. The best ideas in this role aren't in any recruiting playbook you've read.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Who you are</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You sell a mission, not a job.</strong> Candidates leave a conversation with you believing in Hera's mission and their specific place in it. You can hold the whole company narrative in your head, and you quickly adapt as our narrative evolves.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a hunter.</strong> You'd rather build a pipeline from zero than manage inbound. You're relentless on sourcing, fluent with AI tools, and treat \"no response\" as the start of a sequence, not the end of one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've run full-cycle recruiting.</strong> You've closed candidates across technical and non-technical roles, and you know that a founding engineer, a clinician, and a BD lead each need a completely different pitch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You obsess over candidate experience.</strong> You know every interaction is brand-building, and that how we treat the people we don't hire says as much about us as how we treat the ones we do.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a builder.</strong> You thrive bringing clarity to ambiguity. You track your own metrics, you're rigorous about what's working, and you iterate without being told.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You read people deeply.</strong> You catch the hesitation a candidate hasn't said out loud and know whether it's comp, conviction, or a partner in another city.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in NYC or willing to relocate.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What we value</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Worthy of our parents.</strong> We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration must be an accelerant.</strong> Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Celebrate human.</strong> Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enjoy the uphill.</strong> Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attack.</strong> Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:jenny@hellohera.com\">jenny@hellohera.com</a></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"THE GAP NO ONE HAS FILLED\n\nEvery complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.\n\n99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated care manager for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM IS EVERYTHING\n\nWe’re cultivating a team that can run through walls together to take care of the generation that raised us. The DNA of our team and the bar we hold for each other will shape the trajectory of the company. You will craft every touchpoint our future team experiences and how they spend time getting to know us. This is one of the most important roles at the company.\n\n\n\n\nOUR FOUNDING TEAM\n\nWe've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'ed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.\n\nYou'll build Hera alongside co-founders Jenny https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/, Myles https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/ & Connie https://www.linkedin.com/in/conniejkang/ and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you would have meaningful ownership in the company. We are in person in NYC. Read our story here https://hellohera.com/about.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nYou are my right hand on talent. Recruiting at Hera isn't a support function, it's how we win. You'll sit close enough to the founders to know exactly why each role is critical, how our narrative is evolving week to week, and how to tell that story to the exact person we need in the room. When the pitch shifts, you shift with it. When a candidate hesitates, you know which thread to pull.\n\nOwn the entire funnel. Sourcing, screening, and closing end to end, across both technical and business roles. You run the process, you own the candidate experience, and you make every hiring manager better at their part of it. The founding team will stay deeply involved in hiring; your job is to multiply us, not replace us.\n\nHunt. We're still early in building our talent brand, which means the best people won't come to us, you go get them. You have real hunter DNA and you source in an AI-native way: you use every tool available to find, reach, and win people nobody else is finding. Volume without craft doesn't work here, and craft without volume doesn't either.\n\nPartner on talent strategy. You help shape which roles we open, in what order, and what great looks like for each. You bring rigor to how we run loops, calibrate bars, make decisions, and you push back when we're wrong.\n\nMake how we recruit as distinctive as what we're building. We've thrown a talent show where every act is over 65 https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==, sold out all the work for a retired 88 year old who had never sold a piece of art until the art show https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time we threw him, are hosting a Dinner with Nonna series, and have many events coming up that helps us share our story with the world. These are also mediums to bring talent into our community. We want to partner to be unconventional and willing to try things other nobody else has tried. The best ideas in this role aren't in any recruiting playbook you've read.\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You sell a mission, not a job. Candidates leave a conversation with you believing in Hera's mission and their specific place in it. You can hold the whole company narrative in your head, and you quickly adapt as our narrative evolves.\n\n - You're a hunter. You'd rather build a pipeline from zero than manage inbound. You're relentless on sourcing, fluent with AI tools, and treat \"no response\" as the start of a sequence, not the end of one.\n\n - You've run full-cycle recruiting. You've closed candidates across technical and non-technical roles, and you know that a founding engineer, a clinician, and a BD lead each need a completely different pitch.\n\n - You obsess over candidate experience. You know every interaction is brand-building, and that how we treat the people we don't hire says as much about us as how we treat the ones we do.\n\n - You're a builder. You thrive bringing clarity to ambiguity. You track your own metrics, you're rigorous about what's working, and you iterate without being told.\n\n - You read people deeply. You catch the hesitation a candidate hasn't said out loud and know whether it's comp, conviction, or a partner in another city.\n\n - Based in NYC or willing to relocate.\n   \n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Worthy of our parents. We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.\n\n - Collaboration must be an accelerant. Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.\n\n - Celebrate human. Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.\n\n - Enjoy the uphill. Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.\n\n - Attack. Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.\n\n - Our promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: jenny@hellohera.com","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$130K – $240K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$130K - $240K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"10120221-3535-4572-a2fe-c9fc244800d3","tierSummary":"$130K – $240K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4c869f49-1c4e-418d-86f2-24868356d0fe","summary":"$130K – $240K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":240000},{"id":"ac07341c-3be3-4ff9-9ca6-26e4398aaa33","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":240000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a14b6bc1-4816-4bf5-b83f-aa7d0ffe21fa","title":"Onboarding Guide (Patient Enrollment)","department":"Onboarding","team":"Onboarding","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T18:12:22.014+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/a14b6bc1-4816-4bf5-b83f-aa7d0ffe21fa","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/a14b6bc1-4816-4bf5-b83f-aa7d0ffe21fa/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A doctor refers a family to Hera. They're cautiously optimistic but mostly overwhelmed - they've been bounced between systems, handed pamphlets, told to \"call this number.\" They don't know what geriatric care management is. They definitely don't know it's covered by Medicare. They're one confusing phone call away from saying \"never mind, we'll figure it out ourselves.\"</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're the reason they don't.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Onboarding Guide, you're the first voice a family hears from Hera. You help them understand how Hera competently cares for their parents, walk them through every step of getting started, and hand them off to their Hero feeling confident, heard, and ready. You're part closer, part concierge, part care coordinator. You just make the path so clear and the experience so easy that saying yes feels obvious.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of relationship-building and operations. You're selling, but what you're selling is something families genuinely need, and your job is to remove every obstacle between a referral and a first appointment. Missing paperwork, skeptical adult children, a patient who's never used a computer - you will get through whatever it takes so that the family can meet their Hero.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your mission as the Onboarding Guide</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're the reason families actually get help instead of falling through the cracks between referral and care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You aren’t just going through a motion. You're building trust with real families at a vulnerable moment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You own the full onboarding experience, no handing things off and hoping for the best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You leverage technology to make onboarding seamless, not a stack of faxes and voicemails</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Elevate your ceiling. We're early stage and growing fast - Guides joining now are shaping how every future family experiences Hera</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1099 flexibility, 30–40 hrs/week in business hours EST (you set your schedule)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$25-30/hour base + enrollment bonuses (<strong>top performers earn $40-50/hour</strong>)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the first point of contact after a doctor refers a family to Hera - guide them from \"what is Hera?\" to their first Hero appointment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote - must be located in the United States</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll actually do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Convert referrals into active clients by helping families understand what Hera is and how we can be valuable in their care journey</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide families through the onboarding process - paperwork, documentation, insurance verification, scheduling - so nothing stalls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate between families and Hera's care team to ensure a clean handoff to their matched Hero</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help families navigate technology: uploading documents, joining telehealth appointments, signing e-forms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spot friction in the intake process and fix it - not just for one family, but for every family after them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with our engineering team to streamline workflows and scale how many families we can onboard without sacrificing quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'd be a great fit if you</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have a background in healthcare sales, care coordination, or customer success — especially with older adults or their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are warm on the phone and sharp on the follow-through. Families trust you quickly and nothing falls through the cracks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Think \"how do I get this from 2 hours to 15 minutes\" without cutting corners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold yourself to a high bar: done right, not just done</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are tech-savvy and energized by fast-moving environments where the playbook is still being written</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're on a mission to change the way we care for our parents and redefine a universal human experience. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUGD6cawQfk\">Watch our launch video here.</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"A doctor refers a family to Hera. They're cautiously optimistic but mostly overwhelmed - they've been bounced between systems, handed pamphlets, told to \"call this number.\" They don't know what geriatric care management is. They definitely don't know it's covered by Medicare. They're one confusing phone call away from saying \"never mind, we'll figure it out ourselves.\"\n\nYou're the reason they don't.\n\nAs an Onboarding Guide, you're the first voice a family hears from Hera. You help them understand how Hera competently cares for their parents, walk them through every step of getting started, and hand them off to their Hero feeling confident, heard, and ready. You're part closer, part concierge, part care coordinator. You just make the path so clear and the experience so easy that saying yes feels obvious.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of relationship-building and operations. You're selling, but what you're selling is something families genuinely need, and your job is to remove every obstacle between a referral and a first appointment. Missing paperwork, skeptical adult children, a patient who's never used a computer - you will get through whatever it takes so that the family can meet their Hero.\n\nYour mission as the Onboarding Guide\n\n - You're the reason families actually get help instead of falling through the cracks between referral and care\n\n - You aren’t just going through a motion. You're building trust with real families at a vulnerable moment\n\n - You own the full onboarding experience, no handing things off and hoping for the best\n\n - You leverage technology to make onboarding seamless, not a stack of faxes and voicemails\n\n - Elevate your ceiling. We're early stage and growing fast - Guides joining now are shaping how every future family experiences Hera\n\nThe Role\n\n - 1099 flexibility, 30–40 hrs/week in business hours EST (you set your schedule)\n\n - $25-30/hour base + enrollment bonuses (top performers earn $40-50/hour)\n\n - Be the first point of contact after a doctor refers a family to Hera - guide them from \"what is Hera?\" to their first Hero appointment\n\n - Remote - must be located in the United States\n\nWhat you'll actually do\n\n - Convert referrals into active clients by helping families understand what Hera is and how we can be valuable in their care journey\n\n - Guide families through the onboarding process - paperwork, documentation, insurance verification, scheduling - so nothing stalls\n\n - Coordinate between families and Hera's care team to ensure a clean handoff to their matched Hero\n\n - Help families navigate technology: uploading documents, joining telehealth appointments, signing e-forms\n\n - Spot friction in the intake process and fix it - not just for one family, but for every family after them\n\n - Collaborate with our engineering team to streamline workflows and scale how many families we can onboard without sacrificing quality\n\nYou'd be a great fit if you\n\n - Have a background in healthcare sales, care coordination, or customer success — especially with older adults or their families\n\n - Are warm on the phone and sharp on the follow-through. Families trust you quickly and nothing falls through the cracks\n\n - Think \"how do I get this from 2 hours to 15 minutes\" without cutting corners\n\n - Hold yourself to a high bar: done right, not just done\n\n - Are tech-savvy and energized by fast-moving environments where the playbook is still being written\n\nWe're on a mission to change the way we care for our parents and redefine a universal human experience. Watch our launch video here. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUGD6cawQfk","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$25 – $50 per hour • Top performers earn $40-50 / hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"e066d2cb-e164-418d-aee7-6d15752ce0c5","tierSummary":"base + enrollment bonus $25 – $50 per hour • Top performers earn $40-50 / hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":"Top performers earn $40-50 / hour","components":[{"id":"944122cb-482e-444e-9077-cd087b1b32b9","summary":"base + enrollment bonus $25 – $50 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":50}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":50}]}},{"id":"6dba9539-c3de-495d-b38f-c7b2bdac6813","title":"Founding Growth Marketer","department":"Founding Team","team":"Founding Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T17:58:01.982+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/6dba9539-c3de-495d-b38f-c7b2bdac6813","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/6dba9539-c3de-495d-b38f-c7b2bdac6813/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>The gap no one has filled</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated care manager for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Meeting very family that needs a Hero</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The demand for Hera is real, raw, and palpable. Families come to us in the hardest experience of their lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, we meet most of them through their doctors: a strategic channel we've built through close partnerships with the country's top health systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">But millions of families never receive that introduction. Instead, it’s an adult daughter opening her laptop late at night after putting her children to bed, overwhelmed and burnt out. She’s awake searching at midnight about what options exist for her mom, anxious about every decision she’s making and wondering if it’s the right one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">She doesn’t know a trusted profession like ours exists. Nobody’s told her that she doesn’t have to figure this out alone.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is not a traditional growth role. Families don’t know the category exists, don’t know what to search for, and often don’t understand how a Hero could help. It’s our responsibility to educate the market and meet them in the moment they’re looking for help. It’s also the most emotionally charged experience of their life. Every touchpoint has to earn trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Our founding team</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’ve raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x’d revenue over the last six months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. The CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. Along the way, we threw an art show for an 88-year-old artist that <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time\">went viral</a> and a <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?igsh=MTR3cjg4ZmJvb2NyZQ%3D%3D\">talent show</a> where every act was over 65.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll build Hera alongside co-founders <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/\">Jenny</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/\">Myles</a>, and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/\">Connie</a>, and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you will have meaningful ownership in the company. We work together in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.com/about\">here</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You own how families find Hera. You’ll build our consumer growth engine from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deeply understand who we serve.</strong> You’ll immerse and fully understand the mental model of those we support, the trigger events where they think “I can’t do this alone”, the communities and resources they turn to for answers, and the hesitations that linger at the back of their mind before they say yes to support.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Educate the market.</strong> No one knows what to search for. They’re looking for answers on what’s going on in their life right now “mom keeps falling”, “dad was just discharged from the hospital”, “mom keeps mixing up her meds”. You will find the language that makes Hera instantly understandable,</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the family demand engine.</strong> You’ll build and run our direct-to-family channels across search, content, community, social, and more. You’ll own the full funnel: how families learn about us, what convinces them to trust us, and what gets them to reach out.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experiment relentlessly, and do it with a flair.</strong> Everything we do at Hera is distinctive. We threw an art show for an 88-year-old that went viral and a talent show where every act is over 65. We want the same originality in how we build demand. You'll ship scrappy tests fast, kill what doesn't work without ego, and double down on what does. The best ideas in this role aren't in any growth playbook you've read.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Who you are</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re analytical and truth seeking.</strong> You know the difference between a metric moving in the right direction and a future growth channel of the business. You understand unit economics and make commercially sound decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re creative and generative.</strong> We don’t just do things because others do. You constantly produce new hypotheses, messages, campaigns, and channels to find the one that’s authentic to us and really works to scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re obsessed with the customer.</strong> Quant tells you what; qual tells you why. You'll sit with families, listen to calls, and read every message before you write a single headline. You can hold both the spreadsheet and the story of the overwhelmed daughter in your head at once.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a builder with incredible pace.</strong> You thrive bringing clarity to ambiguity. You aim to learn quickly through scrappy experiments and add rigor once something works.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You understand trust is the asset.</strong> We serve a vulnerable population in the hardest moment of their lives. You'd never trade long-term trust for a short-term conversion, because you know trust is the moat and growth compounds on top of it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Based in NYC or willing to relocate</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What we value</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Worthy of our parents.</strong> We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration must be an accelerant.</strong> Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Celebrate human.</strong> Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enjoy the uphill.</strong> Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attack.</strong> Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:jenny@hellohera.com\">jenny@hellohera.com</a></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"THE GAP NO ONE HAS FILLED\n\nEvery complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. A lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare, a trillion-dollar industry that touches every single family, leaves us on our own.\n\n99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that last mile gap: the Hero, a dedicated care manager for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.\n\n\n\n\nMEETING VERY FAMILY THAT NEEDS A HERO\n\nThe demand for Hera is real, raw, and palpable. Families come to us in the hardest experience of their lives.\n\nToday, we meet most of them through their doctors: a strategic channel we've built through close partnerships with the country's top health systems.\n\nBut millions of families never receive that introduction. Instead, it’s an adult daughter opening her laptop late at night after putting her children to bed, overwhelmed and burnt out. She’s awake searching at midnight about what options exist for her mom, anxious about every decision she’s making and wondering if it’s the right one.\n\nShe doesn’t know a trusted profession like ours exists. Nobody’s told her that she doesn’t have to figure this out alone.\n\nThis is not a traditional growth role. Families don’t know the category exists, don’t know what to search for, and often don’t understand how a Hero could help. It’s our responsibility to educate the market and meet them in the moment they’re looking for help. It’s also the most emotionally charged experience of their life. Every touchpoint has to earn trust.\n\n\n\n\nOUR FOUNDING TEAM\n\nWe’ve raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x’d revenue over the last six months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. The CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.\n\nThe customer feedback is the most positive our team has seen in our careers. Along the way, we threw an art show for an 88-year-old artist that went viral https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/02/19/88-year-old-brooklyn-painter-sells-art-for-the-first-time and a talent show https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi3YmESZ6Q/?igsh=MTR3cjg4ZmJvb2NyZQ%3D%3D where every act was over 65.\n\nYou’ll build Hera alongside co-founders Jenny https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennydlee/, Myles https://www.linkedin.com/in/mylesnovick/, and Connie https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingyi-connie-kang/, and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you will have meaningful ownership in the company. We work together in person in NYC. Read our story and watch our launch video here https://hellohera.com/about.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nYou own how families find Hera. You’ll build our consumer growth engine from the ground up.\n\nDeeply understand who we serve. You’ll immerse and fully understand the mental model of those we support, the trigger events where they think “I can’t do this alone”, the communities and resources they turn to for answers, and the hesitations that linger at the back of their mind before they say yes to support.\n\nEducate the market. No one knows what to search for. They’re looking for answers on what’s going on in their life right now “mom keeps falling”, “dad was just discharged from the hospital”, “mom keeps mixing up her meds”. You will find the language that makes Hera instantly understandable,\n\nOwn the family demand engine. You’ll build and run our direct-to-family channels across search, content, community, social, and more. You’ll own the full funnel: how families learn about us, what convinces them to trust us, and what gets them to reach out.\n\nExperiment relentlessly, and do it with a flair. Everything we do at Hera is distinctive. We threw an art show for an 88-year-old that went viral and a talent show where every act is over 65. We want the same originality in how we build demand. You'll ship scrappy tests fast, kill what doesn't work without ego, and double down on what does. The best ideas in this role aren't in any growth playbook you've read.\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You’re analytical and truth seeking. You know the difference between a metric moving in the right direction and a future growth channel of the business. You understand unit economics and make commercially sound decisions.\n\n - You’re creative and generative. We don’t just do things because others do. You constantly produce new hypotheses, messages, campaigns, and channels to find the one that’s authentic to us and really works to scale.\n\n - You’re obsessed with the customer. Quant tells you what; qual tells you why. You'll sit with families, listen to calls, and read every message before you write a single headline. You can hold both the spreadsheet and the story of the overwhelmed daughter in your head at once.\n\n - You're a builder with incredible pace. You thrive bringing clarity to ambiguity. You aim to learn quickly through scrappy experiments and add rigor once something works.\n\n - You understand trust is the asset. We serve a vulnerable population in the hardest moment of their lives. You'd never trade long-term trust for a short-term conversion, because you know trust is the moat and growth compounds on top of it.\n\n - Based in NYC or willing to relocate\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Worthy of our parents. We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.\n\n - Collaboration must be an accelerant. Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.\n\n - Celebrate human. Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.\n\n - Enjoy the uphill. Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.\n\n - Attack. Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.\n\n - Our promise is we will stretch your limits and trust you to own unreasonably substantial outcomes. If this speaks to you, let's talk: jenny@hellohera.com","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f06fd38d-21de-4c0c-8c3e-c50660ae4823","tierSummary":"$150K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0676720f-f850-4ed6-b34a-d2c502460a8f","summary":"$150K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"82348f2b-e75d-4dfb-9225-3cc71be9d290","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a13a392f-530a-4dd8-bfd6-346054f5d022","title":"Product Designer, Family Experience","department":"Founding Team","team":"Founding Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T20:32:58.420+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/a13a392f-530a-4dd8-bfd6-346054f5d022","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/hellohera/a13a392f-530a-4dd8-bfd6-346054f5d022/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><br /><strong>Why Hera exists</strong></h1><h2><br /><strong>The gap no one has filled</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. You have a lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare — a trillion-dollar industry that's arguably the most complex and touches every single family — leaves us on our own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population in the healthcare system. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.<br /></p><h2><strong>The most trusted interface for healthcare</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In the hardest moment of their lives, families run from doctor to doctor and appointment to appointment, hours on the phone, one dead end after another, with no one place to turn. Every other complex system gives you someone to call first. Healthcare doesn't.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hera is that place. We’re building the most trusted surface in healthcare, where families go first during the hardest moments of their lives. In the moment of a discharge, a diagnosis, a fall, Hera is immediately at work. We serve people most technology overlooks: aging parents, their families, and the social workers and nurses who care for them. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">That's why this role exists. You'll design this surface: how families reach us, and how care and support show up in the hardest moments of their lives. You'll turn fear, stress, and overwhelm into clarity and trust: the agent driving real-time guidance and coordination, and humans stepping in when it matters most. You’ll define the shape of the product as the modality of human–agent interaction is being reinvented in real time (think Instinct, Grok bots). The answer for an 82-year-old and their daughter won’t be a dashboard, it’s yours to discover.</p><h2><br /><strong>Our founding team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'ed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. The CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be the second designer on the team, build Hera alongside Ellen, co-founders Jenny, Myles &amp; Connie and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you would be an owner in the company. We are in person in NYC. Read our story <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://hellohera.com/about\">here</a>.</p><h1><br /><strong>The role</strong></h1><h2><br /><strong>Senior Product Designer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll be Hera’s second designer, partnering closely with our Head of Design Ellen. You’ll own the end-to-end family experience — from first touch through the core product.</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the 0→1 family product.</strong> You’ll design the interface where families first meet Hera, in the hardest moments of their lives. This product doesn’t exist yet. You’ll shape it while human–agent interaction is being reinvented in real time (think Instinct, Grok bot)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own a slice of Hera Platform.</strong> Our Heroes and care teams run on the platform we build. You’ll own family-related workflows there (like patient onboarding) that connect directly to the family experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Set the bar for craft and quality.</strong> You’ll help evolve the design system and standards that keep every surface worthy of the brand promise as we scale.</p></li></ol><h2><br /><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re a product designer.</strong> You can take an ambiguous problem, find the sharp edge, and ship software that moves outcomes, even without a dedicated PM.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You set the bar for craft.</strong> You have strong visual judgment and a high standard for interaction, copy, and final polish and you can explain the “why” behind your decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re comfortable in the code.</strong> You work closely with engineering (and can work in a modern codebase when needed) to ensure what ships matches the intended look &amp; feel.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You build systems, not one-offs.</strong> You’ve built or meaningfully expanded a design system and you treat it like a product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You design for trust.</strong> You’ve worked in high-stakes contexts (healthcare, finance, caregiving, etc.) and can show how your decisions earn trust in emotionally loaded moments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ve operated in strong product-led environments:</strong> High-craft teams, fast iteration, close partnership with engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in NYC or willing to relocate.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What we value</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Worthy of our parents.</strong> We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration must be an accelerant.</strong> Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Celebrate human.</strong> Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enjoy the uphill.</strong> Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attack.</strong> Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"\nWHY HERA EXISTS\n\n\n\nTHE GAP NO ONE HAS FILLED\n\nEvery complex system in America has a profession whose job it is to be your trusted guide. You have a lawyer for legal. An accountant for taxes. A financial advisor for your money. Healthcare — a trillion-dollar industry that's arguably the most complex and touches every single family — leaves us on our own.\n\n99% of care happens when someone steps outside the four walls of a doctor's office. Hera is creating a new profession in healthcare to fill that gap: the Hero, a dedicated senior care expert for your family. Our Heroes educate, coordinate, and advocate for the most vulnerable population in the healthcare system. We're covered by insurance, so we can serve every family in America.\n\n\n\nTHE MOST TRUSTED INTERFACE FOR HEALTHCARE\n\nIn the hardest moment of their lives, families run from doctor to doctor and appointment to appointment, hours on the phone, one dead end after another, with no one place to turn. Every other complex system gives you someone to call first. Healthcare doesn't.\n\nHera is that place. We’re building the most trusted surface in healthcare, where families go first during the hardest moments of their lives. In the moment of a discharge, a diagnosis, a fall, Hera is immediately at work. We serve people most technology overlooks: aging parents, their families, and the social workers and nurses who care for them. \n\nThat's why this role exists. You'll design this surface: how families reach us, and how care and support show up in the hardest moments of their lives. You'll turn fear, stress, and overwhelm into clarity and trust: the agent driving real-time guidance and coordination, and humans stepping in when it matters most. You’ll define the shape of the product as the modality of human–agent interaction is being reinvented in real time (think Instinct, Grok bots). The answer for an 82-year-old and their daughter won’t be a dashboard, it’s yours to discover.\n\n\n\nOUR FOUNDING TEAM\n\nWe've raised $34M from Accel and Bain Capital Ventures and 10x'ed revenue over the last 6 months organically through close partnerships with Weill Cornell, NYU Langone, UCSF, USC, and Mount Sinai. The Chief of Geriatrics at Weill Cornell and Director of Geriatrics at NYU Langone have joined us as clinical advisors. The CFO of Mount Sinai has invested in us.\n\nYou'll be the second designer on the team, build Hera alongside Ellen, co-founders Jenny, Myles & Connie and a team from Palantir and Headway. As part of our founding team, you would be an owner in the company. We are in person in NYC. Read our story here https://hellohera.com/about.\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\n\n\nSENIOR PRODUCT DESIGNER\n\nYou’ll be Hera’s second designer, partnering closely with our Head of Design Ellen. You’ll own the end-to-end family experience — from first touch through the core product.\n\n 1. Own the 0→1 family product. You’ll design the interface where families first meet Hera, in the hardest moments of their lives. This product doesn’t exist yet. You’ll shape it while human–agent interaction is being reinvented in real time (think Instinct, Grok bot)\n\n 2. Own a slice of Hera Platform. Our Heroes and care teams run on the platform we build. You’ll own family-related workflows there (like patient onboarding) that connect directly to the family experience.\n\n 3. Set the bar for craft and quality. You’ll help evolve the design system and standards that keep every surface worthy of the brand promise as we scale.\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You’re a product designer. You can take an ambiguous problem, find the sharp edge, and ship software that moves outcomes, even without a dedicated PM.\n\n - You set the bar for craft. You have strong visual judgment and a high standard for interaction, copy, and final polish and you can explain the “why” behind your decisions.\n\n - You’re comfortable in the code. You work closely with engineering (and can work in a modern codebase when needed) to ensure what ships matches the intended look & feel.\n\n - You build systems, not one-offs. You’ve built or meaningfully expanded a design system and you treat it like a product.\n\n - You design for trust. You’ve worked in high-stakes contexts (healthcare, finance, caregiving, etc.) and can show how your decisions earn trust in emotionally loaded moments.\n\n - You’ve operated in strong product-led environments: High-craft teams, fast iteration, close partnership with engineering.\n\n - Based in NYC or willing to relocate.\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Worthy of our parents. We don't leave the 20% behind, because that applies to someone's mother. Quality isn't a constraint we tolerate on the path to growth. Quality is the strategy.\n\n - Collaboration must be an accelerant. Not everything will be collaborated on and that's fine. We assume good intent always and push the ball forward.\n\n - Celebrate human. Humans are at the heart of everything we do: every product decision, every Hero we choose to hire, every person we bring onto the team. For us, empathy is fuel to move with urgency because we know every single day matters for those we serve. We look for missionaries not mercenaries.\n\n - Enjoy the uphill. Wrestling problems this hard, in an industry this broken, is a privilege most people never get. We're excited for the summit but the joy is in the climb. If the hard part isn't what's pulling you, this might be the wrong climb.\n\n - Attack. Nothing is created in this world without an extraordinary amount of effort. In order to will the change we want to see in the world, we attack problems and play offense. We're here to win to ensure our customers get the world they deserve.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}